# Commits that changed formatting and nothing else, so `git blame` skips them and
# shows the commit that last changed the code.
#
# GitHub honours this file automatically. Locally it is opt-in, once per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# One full 40-character SHA per line, with the commit's subject above it. Only a
# commit that provably changed no code belongs here — a mechanical sweep
# (rustfmt, import order, assert messages added with no logic touched), never a
# commit that also fixed something. A SHA listed here is a SHA whose authorship
# nobody will find again by blame.
#
